This package is a fork of Cloudflare Computer, `@cloudflare/computer` 0.2.1.

- Upstream: https://github.com/cloudflare/computer, tag
  `@cloudflare/computer@0.2.1`, commit
  849759bbfc23eafbe989b6b158e31ef60a4afb68.
- Imported: `packages/computer` (package root), plus the bundled workspace
  sources `packages/dofs/src` and `packages/rpc/src` under `vendor/`.
  Upstream tests, benchmarks, test harnesses and `dist/` are omitted.
- License: MIT. Upstream's repository-root LICENSE is kept unchanged in
  `LICENSE` and covers the upstream code and the fork changes.

Fork changes to the upstream build:

- `package.json`: renamed to `@fungi.computer/cloudflare-computer`; exact
  dependency pins taken from upstream's 0.2.1 lockfile; build scripts no longer
  build the omitted sibling workspaces.
- `rolldown.config.ts` and `tsconfig.json`: resolve `@cloudflare/dofs` and
  `@cloudflare/computer-rpc` from `vendor/`; the type set drops
  `vitest/globals`.
- `src/backends/worker-shell/script/build-bundle.mjs`: bundle just-bash 3.2.0
  (the release the published 0.2.1 shell groups contain) through the
  `just-bash-shell-bundle` alias.
- `package.json` `build` cleans `dist/` first.
- The worker-shell core group is imported, typed and kept external as
  `@fungi.computer/cloudflare-computer/shell/core`, the package's own name
  (`shell-modules.ts`, `tsconfig.json`, `rolldown.config.ts`).
- capnweb is `@fungi.computer/capnweb` (the capnweb 0.12.0 fork with corrected
  tuple declarations) in `package.json`, `rolldown.config.ts`, `src/stub.ts`,
  `src/backends/container/cloudflare-container.ts` and `vendor/rpc/src`, so the
  package shares one capnweb runtime with its consumers.

With only those build changes, `pnpm run build` reproduces the published
0.2.1 `dist/` apart from content-hash chunk names, source-path comments, and
the patch releases of bundled third-party code that the workspace lockfile
resolves (for example sql.js 1.14.2 for 1.14.1, papaparse 5.7.0 for 5.5.4,
fast-xml-parser 5.11.1 for 5.10.1, smol-toml 1.8.0 for 1.7.1,
which-typed-array 1.1.24 for 1.1.22).

Fork changes to behavior:

- Worker-shell state: `ShellWorker` reports the shell's final `cwd` and
  environment as a `state` event before `exit`; the runtime wire, the event
  codecs and `WorkspaceRuntimeResult.state` carry it, and the type surface
  exports `WorkspaceShellState`. The worker-shell parser rejects a malformed
  `state` frame. The vendored rpc `ExecEvent` and the worker-javascript record
  codec carry the new member so the types stay exhaustive; the
  worker-javascript backend itself never emits it.
